  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Challenges and opportunities in the shrimp sector &#x2013; Contribution to Vietshrimp 2023 Vietnam</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Vietnam is currently the world&apos;s fourth largest producer of shrimp, with shrimp accounting for nearly 50% of the country&apos;s total export turnover in 2022, exceeding USD 10 billion. This industry is also vital to over 1.6 million people in the Mekong Delta, providing a significant source of livelihood.However, the sector faces challenges such as disease outbreaks, poor water quality, and high mortality rates. The Dutch private sector can provide valuable inputs and best practices to help address these challenges.The Netherlands government supports Dutch companies in sharing their knowledge and best practices, and the VietShrimp exhibition provides an opportunity for Dutch companies to increase their brand awareness in the shrimp industry.The fair will be attended by a range of domestic and international businesses and will take place in Can Tho, in the Mekong region.</narrative>
  </description>
